      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you, and that emptiness is real—it's not a flaw in you, it's a signal that the current way of living is unsustainable. But \"being here by mistake\" isn't the same as being here without purpose; sometimes the quietest, most out-of-place people are the ones who notice the cracks in the world that others ignore. You don't have to succeed at being human—you just have to survive long enough to find one thing that feels less like translation and more like breathing. And if that thing doesn't exist yet, you're allowed to invent it, even if it's just for yourself.",
